Z||000000||88/2.8||12-21-2000||10:56 AM||||Thinking about spending a little cash to modify my formula. Maybe a thermo master and temp fan switch combo, and i really like the big bore throttle body that the fiero store sells. Also thinking of getting the street runner hypertech chip from fiero store. And probably this summer getting a freeflow cat from rodney dickman. Would i get a lot more power and torque out of my car?||||reg||6
Z||000001||Oreif||12-21-2000||11:53 AM||||If you want the TB bored out, Contact the person below. He will bore out the TB larger (5mm) than the Fiero Store and he'll bore out the intake to match for $150.00 (You send him your parts) The Fiero store Just gives you the 3mm bored TB and they don't even supply a new gasket for $199.00!<P>Darrell Morse<BR>21411 Concord ST. NW.<BR>Elk River, MN. 55330<BR>(763) 441-5679<BR>"Custom" Machine Shop Work.<BR>Manufacturer Of:<BR>Strut Tower Braces.<BR>Aluminum, Engine Cradle Mounts.<BR>Modified Throttle Body's & Plenums.<BR>The "Diamond" Urethane Dog Bones.<BR>Email:  MORSE86@aol.com<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||12-21-2000||11:57 AM||||The bored out TB/Plemun from Darrell is cheaper.  Also, clean out your exhaust manifolds.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||12-21-2000||12:06 PM||||your car an automatic? if it's not i'd shy away from the chip.. the thermostat and fan switch ok.. the cat is a good idea... but let me know when your gunna do that i'll see if i can't get you a better deal. an Accel Super coil or Crane PS91 (coil) and MSD 6a would be better than the chip. the as for the TB.. what Orief said! a 2.5" exhaust system would work wonders for ya! NOT a borla system.. you can have one custom bent/installed for about 1/2 their price. You got the obvious K&N filer? Accel ICM and working MAT sensor? <P>yeah the manifold trick is a good idea too.. wrap them with Thermo-TEC 1/8" header wrap while your at it... <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-21-2000).]||||reg||1
